Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.35,0:00:05.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,In a home for the elderly, two old men\Nshared one room.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.11,0:00:07.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,The room had a single window.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.56,0:00:11.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ato Girma’s bed was beside it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.17,0:00:16.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ato Kebede lay flat on his back and saw\Nonly the ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.06,0:00:23.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every afternoon, Ato Girma sat up and\Ndescribed everything he could see
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.25,0:00:25.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,through the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.85,0:00:32.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,“I see a garden ringed with beautiful\Ntrees… children chasing a ball.”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.56,0:00:40.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,“Sweethearts walk hand in hand… and\Nbeyond them, I see lovely hills.”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.18,0:00:47.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ato Kebede closed his eyes and saw it\Nall. Weeks went by like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.43,0:00:53.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,One morning, Ato Girma’s bed was empty.\NHe had passed away in the night.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.18,0:01:00.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ato Kebede asked for his bed to be moved\Nto the window. He could not wait to see.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.02,0:01:05.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,But beyond the window there was only a\Nwhite wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.68,0:01:11.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,The caregiver told him, “Ato Girma could\Nnot see. He was blind.”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.56,0:01:17.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,He had invented it all, to give his\Nfriend the hope to go on living.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.08,0:01:21.08,Card,,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,0)}{\fs88\b1}The Window{\b0\fs59}\N\NMade with AI
